  "grammar": [
    {
      "id": "b3_u04_l1_g1",
      "pattern": "A/V-ㅂ니다/습니다, N입니다",
      "meaning_uz": "Rasmiy uslub (ish suhbati, taqdimot)",
      "meaning_en": "Formal style (interviews, presentations)",
      "explanation_md": "**-ㅂ니다/습니다** (1-kitob 2-2 da tanishgan) — **rasmiy** nutq. Ish suhbatida, taqdimotda, yangiliklarda shu uslub kutiladi.\n\n**컴퓨터 회사에서 일한 적이 있습니다.** — *Kompyuter kompaniyasida ishlaganman.*\n\n### Shakllar\n\n| | Hozirgi | O'tgan | So'roq |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 받침siz | 합니다 | 했습니다 | 합니까? |\n| 받침 bilan | 있습니다 | 있었습니다 | 있습니까? |\n| Ot | 학생입니다 | 학생이었습니다 | 학생입니까? |\n\n### Rasmiy iboralar\n\n- **-겠습니다** — kamtar va'da: **열심히 하겠습니다.** — *Tirishib ishlayman.*\n- **-(으)십시오** — rasmiy iltimos: **앉으십시오.** — *O'tiring.*\n- **무엇입니까?** = **뭐예요?** ning rasmiy shakli.\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- Suhbatda boshidan oxirigacha bir uslubda gapiring — rasmiy va oddiy uslubni aralashtirmang.",
      "explanation_md_en": "**-ㅂ니다/습니다** (first seen in book 1, 2-2) is **formal** speech. It's expected in job interviews, presentations and the news.\n\n**컴퓨터 회사에서 일한 적이 있습니다.** — *I have worked at a computer company.*\n\n### Forms\n\n| | Present | Past | Question |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| no 받침 | 합니다 | 했습니다 | 합니까? |\n| with 받침 | 있습니다 | 있었습니다 | 있습니까? |\n| noun | 학생입니다 | 학생이었습니다 | 학생입니까? |\n\n### Formal phrases\n\n- **-겠습니다** — a humble promise: **열심히 하겠습니다.** — *I'll do my best.*\n- **-(으)십시오** — a formal request: **앉으십시오.** — *Please be seated.*\n- **무엇입니까?** is the formal **뭐예요?**\n\n### Remember\n\n- Keep one style throughout an interview — don't mix formal and casual polite.",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "Hozirgi",
          "condition_en": "Present",
          "rule": "-ㅂ니다/습니다",
          "example": "합니다, 있습니다"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "O'tgan",
          "condition_en": "Past",
          "rule": "-았/었습니다",
          "example": "했습니다, 일했습니다"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Ot",
          "condition_en": "Noun",
          "rule": "N입니다",
          "example": "신입 사원입니다"
        },
        {
